main/ and spiffs/

These files are derived from the "usb_msc_wireless_disk" example of
esp-iot-solution:
  https://github.com/espressif/esp-iot-solution/tree/master/examples/usb/device/usb_msc_wireless_disk
Copyright Espressif Systems (Shanghai) CO LTD, licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. Original SPDX headers have been retained.

Changes made to the original example (see CLAUDE.md for details):
  - Adapted for the ESP32-S3 KEY V1.0 USB dongle, including SDMMC pinout
    for an external microSD card (4-bit SDIO).
  - Added an automatic USB "media changed" soft-reconnect, implemented by
    briefly toggling the native USB-OTG VBUS-valid signal
    (msc_notify_media_change()), so an embroidery machine picks up files
    added or removed via the web interface without unplugging. Triggered
    after upload/delete and exposed manually via GET /reset_msc.
  - Updated esp_wifi_set_config() calls from the deprecated
    ESP_IF_WIFI_AP/ESP_IF_WIFI_STA to WIFI_IF_AP/WIFI_IF_STA for
    ESP-IDF 6.0.
  - Adjusted FATFS/SD card and WiFi defaults (FAT32-focused configuration,
    SoftAP SSID/password) for this project's use case.

